5 Hidden inverses as an error mitigation protocol for applications: variational quantum eigensolvers
5.1 Hamiltonian and Ansatz
Variational quantum eigensolvers (VQE) are
a successful cornerstone of hybrid quantumclassical algorithms explored on NISQ era machines. For a given system Hamiltonian H, and
parameterized ansatz |Ψ(α)i, the ground state
and its energy are obtained by classically minimizing the energy,
